.TITLE "diff"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Compares two files line by line and displays the __differences__ between them. It is an essential tool for __code review__ and tracking changes in configuration files.

.DIV "TLDR"
**diff file1 file2**
Displays the lines that are different between two files.
> __file1__ first file | __file2__ second file

**diff -u file1 file2**
Displays the differences in a unified format, which is easier for humans to read.
> __-u__ unified format flag | __file1__ first file | __file2__ second file

**diff -r folder1 folder2**
Recursively compares the contents of two directories.
> __-r__ recursive flag | __folder1__ first directory | __folder2__ second directory

**diff -i file1 file2**
Ignores case differences when comparing the contents of the files.
> __-i__ ignore case flag | __file1__ first file | __file2__ second file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
The unified format (__-u__) is the standard format used for creating patches. Using __diff__ helps you quickly identify exactly what has changed between two versions of a file before committing or applying updates.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:patch** **cli:cmp** **cli:comm**

